# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
# The marking golden set: photographs of real people's handwriting, and David's
# hand-marking of them. Personal data of minors and of the volunteers who wrote
# it, and the ground truth we grade ourselves against — read-only reference,
# like the past papers. Never in the repo.
design/golden/
# The CXC past papers, specimen and subject reports. Read, never kept: they are
# CXC's copyright and the standing rule is that no past-paper content enters
# this repo. They were tracked for months anyway — 29 files, 94MB — because the
# comment above said "like the past papers" while the rule below only named the
# golden set. Ignored explicitly now so that `git add -A` cannot sweep them back
# in, which is exactly how they returned once already.
design/reference/
